{"assets":["/statement-assets/c99fcddec39e07b2238777c823bafa10d615d43c6dfe89f806ed6d3de213ba20.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1194","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Remove a Progression"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have a list of numbers from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ written from left to right on the blackboard."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You perform an algorithm consisting of several steps (steps are $$$1$$$-indexed). On the $$$i$$$-th step you wipe the $$$i$$$-th number (considering only "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"remaining"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" numbers). You wipe "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"the whole number"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" (not one digit)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/c99fcddec39e07b2238777c823bafa10d615d43c6dfe89f806ed6d3de213ba20.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"When there are less than $$$i$$$ numbers remaining, you stop your algorithm. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now you wonder: what is the value of the $$$x$$$-th remaining number after the algorithm is stopped?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains one integer $$$T$$$ ($$$1 \\le T \\le 100$$$) — the number of queries. The next $$$T$$$ lines contain queries — one per line. All queries are independent."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each line contains two space-separated integers $$$n$$$ and $$$x$$$ ($$$1 \\le x \\lt n \\le 10^{9}$$$) — the length of the list and the position we wonder about. It's guaranteed that after the algorithm ends, the list will still contain at least $$$x$$$ numbers."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print $$$T$$$ integers (one per query) — the values of the $$$x$$$-th number after performing the algorithm for the corresponding queries."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n3 1\n4 2\n69 6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n4\n12\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"1194A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1194/problem/A"}